{"repositoryId":1086131962,"availability":"available","full":"plasma4/RuntimeFS","name":"RuntimeFS","description":"RuntimeFS is an IndexedDB and ServiceWorker file-system, served in your browser with offline functionality (like a localhost).","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":5,"forks":2,"created":"2025-10-30T01:50:42Z","updated":"2026-08-05T04:20:24Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://plasma4.org/projects/RuntimeFS/","topics":["filesystem","indexeddb","localhost-related","pwa","service-worker"],"demo":"https://plasma4.org/projects/RuntimeFS/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T01:45:40.865Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T01:45:40.865Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T01:45:40.865Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T21:46:02.731Z","stars":5,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-20T01:45:40.865Z","stars":5,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["RuntimeFS is a no-nonsense OPFS and ServiceWorker file-system, served in your browser, allowing you to import custom folders and access them like a localhost. It allows you to open HTML projects, use some encryption techniques, and comes with full offline and complete .tar.gz or encrypted data export functionality.","Imagine an offline localhost, in your browser with no server-based storage of files. It saves all files and data locally, and can easily be integrated within an existing website too (the code is MIT Licensed, and around 100KB in size).","After the initial page loads, RuntimeFS no longer needs internet connection to function. RuntimeFS also supports in-place opening of files, which doesn't require opening another tab."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/plasma4/RuntimeFS/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0abda2691b6eda1111a9814471cc453fb6f5054eade7718a37bf892f97e37016","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:02.856Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T21:46:02.856Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Runtime